tdesktop-rust (0~git20261002.e59e0d8+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging for ppa:lightofmysoul/tg, superseding tlottie.
  * Telegram Desktop 7.3.0 adds a second Rust dependency, wallet-engine, and
    links every Rust dependency as one static library, tdesktop_rust: two
    Rust staticlibs would each embed the standard library, and the linker
    refuses its global runtime symbols twice. This package builds that
    archive the way prepare.py, the centos_env Dockerfile and snapcraft.yaml
    do: an umbrella crate re-exporting tlottie and wallet-engine, then the
    C++ binding generated by wallet-engine's own uniffi-bindgen-cpp.
  * tlottie 92df98d (v1.0.6) and wallet-engine e59e0d8 (0.0.7), the
    revisions Telegram Desktop v7.3.0 pins, are carried as submodules.
  * Apply wallet-engine.patch from desktop-app/patches aec4749, as 7.3.0
    does. It adds the TL-B decoder that displays TON Connect signData cells.
    tlottie.patch is gone: tlottie 1.0.5 and 1.0.6 fixed the same rlottie
    compatibility issues upstream, and 7.3.0 no longer applies it.
  * Build with resolute's Rust 1.93.1. wallet-engine declares rust-version
    1.96.1 but compiles unchanged, so it builds with --ignore-rust-version;
    the three CPUID calls in tlottie still need unsafe blocks, now a patch
    in debian/patches since tlottie is a submodule.
  * Vendor every crate both lock files and the generator need, with the
    ones no Linux amd64/arm64 build reaches replaced by stubs.
  * libtdesktop-rust-dev conflicts with and replaces libtlottie-dev: it
    ships the same tlottie.h, while libtdesktop_rust.a takes the place of
    libtlottie.a.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
